msgid "You study the stars carefully, but they remain silent."
msgstr "你仔细端详群星，但它们沉默不语。"

msgid "The constellation offers no insight this time."
msgstr "这次星座没有给出任何启示。"

msgid "Whatever message the stars held has slipped away."
msgstr "群星原本承载的讯息已然消逝。"

msgid "You sense a faint presence among the stars, but it quickly fades."
msgstr "你感到星间有一丝微弱的存在，但转瞬即逝。"

msgid "The constellation's light flickers without revealing its secrets."
msgstr "星座的光芒闪了闪，却没有透露它的秘密。"

msgid "You wait patiently for a sign, but none arrives."
msgstr "你耐心等待征兆，却始终没有出现。"

msgid "You almost discern a message before it vanishes from your thoughts."
msgstr "你几乎要看懂那道讯息，它却在思绪中消散了。"

msgid "The constellation politely declines to elaborate."
msgstr "星座礼貌地拒绝多作解释。"

msgid "You feel certain the stars judged your attempt. They offer no further comment."
msgstr "你确信群星评判了你的尝试。它们没有再多说什么。"

msgid "Even the stars have off days."
msgstr "连星星也有状态不佳的时候。"

msgid "You continue to observe the stars, confirming that they are indeed stars."
msgstr "你继续观测群星，确认了它们确实是星星。"

msgid "The stars insist that talking to plants helps. They refuse to comment on whether the plants listen."
msgstr "群星坚称跟植物说话有用。至于植物听不听，它们拒绝评论。"

msgid "The constellation warns that the tallest tree always wins an argument with a blunt axe."
msgstr "星座警告：最粗的树，总能在跟钝斧的争论中获胜。"

msgid "The stars reveal that weeds are simply crops with exceptional confidence."
msgstr "群星揭示：杂草不过是格外自信的作物。"

msgid "The stars suggest that planting today is wiser than promising you'll plant tomorrow."
msgstr "群星建议：今天播种，比承诺明天播种更明智。"

msgid "The constellation claims every mighty Oak Tree was once a seed that ignored terrible advice."
msgstr "星座宣称：每一棵参天橡树，都曾是一颗无视忠告的种子。"

msgid "The stars quietly remind you that chopping the tree before collecting the fruit is rarely the optimal strategy."
msgstr "群星悄悄提醒你：先砍树再采果，很少是个好主意。"

msgid "The stars wonder why you're not mining Coal right now."
msgstr "群星纳闷你现在怎么没在挖煤。"

msgid "The stars insist that hitting the rock harder is a valid mining strategy."
msgstr "群星坚称：把岩石敲得更狠，是一种完全可行的采矿策略。"

msgid "The constellations insists you are one Geode away from finding that rare item."
msgstr "星座坚称：你离那件稀有物品只差一颗晶洞。"

msgid "The stars wonder how staring at them all night helps build Strength."
msgstr "群星纳闷：整夜盯着它们看，怎么就能练出力量。"

msgid "The constellation reminds you that a high Strength level won't save you from the Coal mines."
msgstr "星座提醒你：力量等级再高，也救不了你在煤矿里的处境。"

msgid "The stars stare back at you."
msgstr "群星也回望着你。"

msgid "The stars whisper that fish are far less cooperative once they realize they're on the menu."
msgstr "群星低语：鱼一旦发现自己上了菜单，就没那么配合了。"

msgid "The stars suggest drying your firewood before complaining that it won't burn."
msgstr "群星建议：先把柴火晾干，再抱怨它烧不着。"

msgid "The constellation reminds you that cooking the fish is generally easier after you've caught it."
msgstr "星座提醒你：把鱼钓上来之后，烹饪通常容易得多。"

msgid "The constellation insists that a warm campfire has ended more adventures than any monster."
msgstr "星座坚称：葬送冒险的篝火，比怪物多得多。"

msgid "The stars guide you to a secluded steam within the Shrapnel River."
msgstr "群星指引你找到弹片河中一处隐秘的温泉。"

msgid "The stars guide you to a hidden spot along the Windy Coastline."
msgstr "群星指引你找到多风海岸线上的一处隐秘地点。"

msgid "The constellation claims every perfect hide once belonged to something that strongly preferred keeping it."
msgstr "星座宣称：每一张完美的兽皮，原本都属于一个极不愿交出它的家伙。"

msgid "The constellation wonders why creatures are so attached to materials you clearly need for crafting."
msgstr "星座纳闷：这些生物为何如此看重你显然要拿去制作的材料。"

msgid "The stars remind you that chasing wildlife is considerably easier without carrying half your workshop."
msgstr "群星提醒你：别背着半个作坊去追野兽，会轻松得多。"

msgid "The stars insist that \"I'll just hunt one more\" has misled countless adventurers."
msgstr "群星坚称：「再打一只就走」坑过无数冒险者。"

msgid "The constellation reveals that collecting \"just in case\" materials eventually becomes a storage problem."
msgstr "星座揭示：为「说不定有用」而囤积材料，最后都会变成仓储问题。"

msgid "The constellation lights a path towards a hidden opening in the Hills."
msgstr "星座照亮一条通往丘陵隐秘洞口的路径。"

msgid "The constellation points toward a tranquil lake where the water curves like a crescent moon. A hidden shoreline beckons those willing to seek it."
msgstr "星座指向一片宁静的湖泊，湖水弯如一弯新月。一处隐秘的湖岸正等着愿意寻觅的人。"

msgid "The stars claim that yelling while attacking increases accuracy."
msgstr "群星声称：攻击时大喊能提高命中率。"

msgid "The stars remind you that every dent in your armour is a valuable lesson. Preferably someone else's lesson."
msgstr "群星提醒你：护甲上的每一处凹痕都是宝贵的教训。最好是别人的教训。"

msgid "The constellation claims that missing your target is not a valid strategy."
msgstr "星座宣称：打不中目标，算不上一种策略。"

msgid "The stars claim every unique weapon began life as \"good enough for now.\""
msgstr "群星声称：每一件独一无二的武器，起初都只是「暂时够用」。"

msgid "The stars insist that hitting harder is a perfectly valid strategy."
msgstr "群星坚称：打得更狠，是完全行得通的策略。"

msgid "The constellation claims every arrow flies true until the wind develops a personality."
msgstr "星座宣称：每支箭都飞得笔直，直到风有了自己的脾气。"

msgid "The stars suggest aiming before celebrating the shot."
msgstr "群星建议：先瞄准，再庆祝。"

msgid "The constellation reminds you that trees rarely volunteer to become arrows."
msgstr "星座提醒你：树木很少自愿变成箭。"

msgid "The stars wonder why arrows are always found in the most inconvenient places."
msgstr "群星纳闷：箭为何总出现在最不方便的地方。"

msgid "The constellation claims a quiver is merely a very organised collection of future mistakes."
msgstr "星座宣称：箭袋不过是一堆整理得很整齐的、未来的失误。"

msgid "The constellation advises remembering that boomerangs are designed to return."
msgstr "星座建议你记住：回旋镖本来就是会飞回来的。"

msgid "Placeholder to replace."
msgstr "占位文本，待替换。"

msgid "The stars insist that every spell is perfectly safe until proven otherwise."
msgstr "群星坚称：每个法术在被证明危险之前，都是完全安全的。"

msgid "The constellation wonders why wizards keep writing things down when they can barely read their own spellbooks."
msgstr "星座纳闷：巫师连自己的法术书都看不太懂，为何还老爱记笔记。"

msgid "The heavens insist that magical explosions are merely enthusiastic successes."
msgstr "上天坚称：魔法爆炸不过是热情过头的成功。"

msgid "The stars reveal that every great mage has accidentally cast something they absolutely didn't mean to."
msgstr "群星揭示：每位大法师都曾不小心放出自己完全没想放的东西。"

msgid "The constellation reminds you that staring at it all night won't solve your Rune supply problems."
msgstr "星座提醒你：整夜盯着它看，解决不了你的符文供应问题。"

msgid "You somehow learn a new form of Magic by simply looking at the stars and pretending to read them or something lol."
msgstr "你就这么盯着星星、假装能读懂它们之类的，莫名其妙学会了一种新魔法，笑死。"

msgid "The constellation reveals an ancient rite. Its celestial words awaken the power of Astral Prayers."
msgstr "星座揭示了一段古老仪轨。其中的天界语词唤醒了星界祈祷的力量。"

msgid "The stars reveal that blessed logs burn brighter than ordinary ones. Coincidence, perhaps."
msgstr "群星揭示：受福的原木比普通原木烧得更旺。也许只是巧合。"

msgid "The stars wonder who first looked at a pile of bones and thought, \"The gods will love this.\""
msgstr "群星纳闷：第一个看着一堆骨头想「神明会喜欢这个」的人到底是谁。"

msgid "The constellation insist that divine favour cannot be bought. Offerings, however, are gladly accepted."
msgstr "星座坚称：神恩是买不到的。不过供品嘛，他们很乐意收下。"

msgid "The constellation claims the gods have excellent taste in offerings, though their preferences remain oddly specific."
msgstr "星座宣称：神明的供品品味极佳，只是偏好具体得有点古怪。"

msgid "The constellation observes that the gods rarely explain why they like bones. They simply do."
msgstr "星座如是说：神明很少解释为何喜欢骨头。反正就是喜欢。"

msgid "The stars reveal a crater where moonlight never truly fades. Something ancient still stirs within its scar."
msgstr "群星揭示一处月光永不消散的环形山。那道伤疤之中，仍有古老之物在翻动。"

msgid "The stars wonder where your ingredients go when you fail to cook something."
msgstr "群星纳闷：你烹饪失败时，材料都去了哪里。"

msgid "The constellation claims a hearty meal can solve many problems. The remaining problems usually require a weapon."
msgstr "星座宣称：一顿饱饭能解决许多问题。剩下的问题通常得靠武器。"

msgid "The constellation insists that eating during a battle is a skill worthy of admiration."
msgstr "星座坚称：战斗中进食是一门值得敬佩的技艺。"

msgid "The stars reveal that a full stomach is often the first step toward surviving the next encounter."
msgstr "群星揭示：肚子填饱，往往是撑过下一场遭遇的第一步。"

msgid "The constellation claims every meal tastes better after narrowly avoiding defeat."
msgstr "星座宣称：死里逃生之后的每一餐都更香。"

msgid "The constellation claims locked doors are merely suggestions."
msgstr "星座宣称：上锁的门不过是种建议。"

msgid "The stars reveal that every graceful landing is built upon countless less graceful ones."
msgstr "群星揭示：每一次优雅落地，都建立在无数次不那么优雅的落地之上。"

msgid "The stars wonder why NPCs cannot pickpocket you as well."
msgstr "群星纳闷：NPC 怎么就不能也来偷你的口袋。"

msgid "The constellation hints at accepting bribes for more Stealth in return."
msgstr "星座暗示：收点贿赂，就能换来更多潜行。"

msgid "The constellation wonders why a very specific item seems to constantly appear on random routes."
msgstr "星座纳闷：为什么某件特定的物品总出现在随机的路线上。"

msgid "The constellation reminds you that it cannot assist with your Lockpick problem."
msgstr "星座提醒你：你的开锁工具问题，它帮不上忙。"

msgid "The stars insist that the best defence is letting the monster become someone else's assignment."
msgstr "群星坚称：最好的防御，是让那只怪物变成别人的任务。"

msgid "The constellation claims every Slayer task looks reasonable until you actually arrive."
msgstr "星座宣称：每个讨伐任务看起来都还算合理，直到你真的到场。"

msgid "The stars reveal that shields are much easier to repair than confidence."
msgstr "群星揭示：修盾比修复自信容易得多。"

msgid "The stars wonder if Slayer Masters secretly compete to invent increasingly inconvenient tasks."
msgstr "群星怀疑：讨伐官们是否暗中较劲，比谁想出的任务更麻烦。"

msgid "The constellation insists that \"just one more monster\" has delayed many journeys home."
msgstr "星座坚称：「再打一只」耽误过无数人回家。"

msgid "The stars reveal that every experienced slayer has confidently attacked the wrong monster at least once."
msgstr "群星揭示：每个老练的讨伐者，都至少自信满满地打错过一次怪物。"

msgid "I think they've gotten the idea."
msgstr "我看他们算是领会了。"

msgid "I knew they'd be bad, but wow."
msgstr "我知道他们会很糟，但没想到这么糟。"

msgid "Let's hope they can figure out how to swing 'em."
msgstr "但愿他们能搞明白怎么抡。"

msgid "What was that?"
msgstr "刚才那是什么？"

msgid "That should be about all of them."
msgstr "大概就这些了。"

msgid "Looking a lot nicer."
msgstr "看起来好多了。"

msgid "Huh, there really is a lot of junk in the water. Wonder where it's coming from?"
msgstr "嘿，水里垃圾还真多。不知道是从哪来的？"

msgid "Maybe Hapren would appreciate the meat?"
msgstr "也许哈普伦会喜欢这些肉？"

msgid "These should work!"
msgstr "这些应该能用！"

msgid "Don't drop them don't drop them don't drop them."
msgstr "别掉别掉别掉。"

msgid "That seems like all of them, for now."
msgstr "目前看来就这些了。"

msgid "I think that should hold!"
msgstr "我觉得这应该撑得住！"

msgid "Hopefully Gloob's contacts pull through."
msgstr "但愿格鲁布的关系能起作用。"

msgid "I don't think anyone heard me."
msgstr "我觉得没人听见我说话。"

msgid "Maybe I should have gone for something more nutritious..."
msgstr "也许我该弄点更有营养的……"

msgid "They're still... moving a bit."
msgstr "它们还……有点在动。"

msgid "Think that's everything!"
msgstr "应该就这些了！"

msgid "It's time."
msgstr "该动手了。"

msgid "There! A hole!"
msgstr "有了！一个洞！"

msgid "It's... done."
msgstr "算是……完事了。"

msgid "[color=green]This observation grants you with access to the Moonlit Stream Fishing spot.[/color]"
msgstr "[color=green]这次观测为你解锁月光溪流钓鱼点。[/color]"

msgid "[color=green]This observation grants you with access to the Midnight Cove Fishing spot.[/color]"
msgstr "[color=green]这次观测为你解锁午夜海湾钓鱼点。[/color]"

msgid "[color=green]This observation grants you with access to the Moonlit Hills Hunting Location.[/color]"
msgstr "[color=green]这次观测为你解锁月光丘陵狩猎地点。[/color]"

msgid "[color=green]This observation grants you with access to the Crescent Lake Combat Area.[/color]"
msgstr "[color=green]这次观测为你解锁新月湖战斗区域。[/color]"

msgid "[color=green]This observation grants you with the knowledge to use Astral Spells.[/color]"
msgstr "[color=green]这次观测赋予你使用星界法术的知识。[/color]"

msgid "[color=green]This observation grants you with the knowledge to use Astral Prayers.[/color]"
msgstr "[color=green]这次观测赋予你使用星界祈祷的知识。[/color]"

msgid "[color=green]This observation grants you with access to the Moonscarred Crater Slayer Zone.[/color]"
msgstr "[color=green]这次观测为你解锁月痕陨坑讨伐区域。[/color]"

msgid "The cinders from the assault on Azamire have only just fizzled out, much like many of the survivors' will to go on. Everyone that remained had lost something. Their homes. Family members. Friends. You and [Companion Name] sit on the soot covered cobbles that once made up the town's main thoroughfare, watching another family carry what little they have left and shuffle out of town, hoping that some nearby village may have been spared. Neither of you blame them.\n\nA woman with a bloodied stump where her hand should have been approaches the two of you and falls to the ground beside you with a sigh."
msgstr "袭击阿扎米尔的余烬才刚熄灭，就像许多幸存者继续活下去的意志一样。留下的人都失去了些什么。家园。亲人。朋友。你和[Companion Name]坐在铺满煤渣的鹅卵石上——这里曾是镇上的主街——看着又一家人带着仅剩的一点东西，拖着脚步离开小镇，指望附近的某个村子逃过一劫。你们都不怪他们。\n\n一个女人走到你们旁边——她本该是手的地方只剩一截血淋淋的残肢——长叹一声，瘫坐在你们身旁。"

msgid "The three of you chat back and forth for a while, putting together the idea of a lesson plan, putting up some ramshackle targets meant to resemble a humanoid figure, and some scavenged gear. Jass brings back a dozen or so dusty villagers from town who seem to carry a wide range of emotions. Some, determined to fight back against the cloaked figures who destroyed the town, some who looked lost and aimless, and some somewhere in between.\n\n[Companion Name] takes half of them and gets to work showing them how to make bows, something they were always better at than actually firing them, while you take the other half and get to work showing them how to make arrows."
msgstr "你们三人来回商量了一阵，凑出一套教学计划，又立起几个破烂的靶子，勉强做出人形，还找了些捡来的装备。贾斯从镇上带回十来个灰头土脸的村民，他们脸上的情绪各式各样：有的下定决心要跟那些毁掉镇子的斗篷人对抗到底，有的茫然无措，还有的介于两者之间。\n\n[Companion Name]领走一半人，开始教他们做弓——这始终是他们比射箭更擅长的本事；你领走另一半，开始教他们做箭。"

msgid "[Companion Name] glares at you, but you've known them long enough to know there's no real anger there, just like they know you have no malice in your light banter.\n\nThough, you start to think otherwise when the villagers pick up their bows and start trying to hit the targets. You feel as though their arrows pass by you more often than the targets. You get to work quickly, trying to show them how to draw, aim, and fire, before they really hurt someone."
msgstr "[Companion Name]瞪着你，但你认识他们这么久，知道那不是真的生气，就像他们也知道你那些玩笑里没有恶意。\n\n只是当村民们拿起弓、试着射靶子时，你开始觉得不对。你总感觉那些箭从你身边飞过的次数比射中靶子还多。你赶紧上前，赶在他们真伤到人之前教他们怎么拉弓、瞄准、放箭。"

msgid "You certainly lost a bit of skin from arrows that passed by a bit too close for comfort, but after a while, the villagers' shots start to resemble straight flight paths. A couple folks pick it up faster than the others, among them, [Companion Name], though you still could hardly say you felt safe just yet.\n\nInitially, Jass seemed to be a bit frustrated at not being able to join in the demonstration, but fell into her own role guiding people and repeating your instructions to those that seemed to struggle the first few times around, or giving pointers that even you started to incorporate into your own shots.\n\nBy the end of the day, the villagers didn't seem to actively be putting one another in danger, and looked far more determined than they did at the start of the drill, and you entrust them into Jass's tutelage, for better or worse."
msgstr "你确实被几支擦身而过的箭蹭掉了一点皮，不过过了一会儿，村民们的箭终于开始像笔直的飞行轨迹了。有几个人学得比别人快，[Companion Name]也在其中——只是你还不敢说自己已经感到安全。\n\n起初贾斯似乎因为没法一起参与示范而有点郁闷，但很快找到了自己的角色：引导大家，把你讲过的要点重复给那些头几次总做不对的人，甚至给出一些连你后来都学着用在自己射术上的诀窍。\n\n到这一天结束时，村民们看起来至少不会主动把彼此弄伤了，神情也比操练刚开始时坚定得多。你把他们交给了贾斯带，好坏都看她了。"

msgid "[Companion Name] leads you to the river where the girl went missing. You fondly recall learning to swim with [Companion Name] here, years ago, and wish you were here under less dire circumstances. The militia disperses through the surrounding forest, headed by Jass who quietly gives orders, trying to get people hidden as best she can.\n\nYou and [Companion Name] settle in by the riverbank, and pull out your rods, hoping to catch a bit more than just a few fish. You're a bit too nervous for idle conversation, so you both quietly fall into a rhythm, just trying to look like two innocuous people fishing late into the night."
msgstr "[Companion Name]带你来到那个女孩失踪的河边。你想起许多年前和[Companion Name]在这里学游泳的事，心里有点暖，又希望这次不是在这种危急关头回来。民兵散入四周的林子，由贾斯领头，她低声下令，尽量把人都藏好。\n\n你和[Companion Name]在河岸边安顿下来，取出鱼竿，盼着能钓上点比鱼更多的东西。你紧张得没心思闲聊，于是两人默默进入节奏，只求看起来像两个在深夜钓鱼的普通路人。"

msgid "You look around as the movement begins to settle. The Golbin force was larger than you had anticipated, but your efforts went as well as could be expected. Among the bodies littering the forest floor, from what you could see, only a couple were human, which was better than expected considering their experience.\n\nYou rush over as you hear a shout from Jass, who managed to pin a dark green Golbin to ground. The beast would have hardly came up to your hip had it been on its feet, and you could hear it whimpering and begging not to be hurt. It quickly rattles off fragments of information that it thinks could be useful, detailing how its clan was taken over by a rival group led by someone it called the 'Ringleader', its own name - Gloob - and how it really really wants to live. Jass slaps her hand over its mouth and asks it where the girl they kidnapped was, and why they took her. Gloob goes one step further, and says that it'll lead you all there to its nearby camp, and that they were going to try and paint him and sell him off too, whatever that may mean.\n\nYou discuss it briefly together, and decide to 'trust' it to do as it says. Surely enough, the camp is close, and the leftover defenders quickly scatter as they see they're vastly outnumbered, leaving their camp behind. You and [Companion Name] quickly find Ana in one of their tents and take her home, while Jass and the militia handle a dozen or so other folks who had been captured from elsewhere throughout the countryside. Ana's mother meets you just outside of Azamire with tears in her eyes, thanking you over and over again for saving her daughter."
msgstr "你环顾四周，骚动渐渐平息。哥布林的数量比你预想的多，但你们的应对已经算得上尽了人事。林地里的尸体中，你能看到的只有两三具是人，考虑到他们的经验，这已经比预想的好。\n\n听到贾斯一声喊，你冲了过去——她把一只深绿色的哥布林按在地上。那东西要是站起来，大概还不到你的腰，你能听见它抽噎着哀求别伤害它。它飞快地吐出一串自认为有用的碎片：它的部族被一伙对手接管，头领被称作「首领」；它自己叫格鲁布；以及它真的真的很想活命。贾斯一把捂住它的嘴，问它他们把抓走的女孩带去了哪里、为什么要抓她。格鲁布更进一步，说它可以带你们去附近的营地，还说他们打算把它也涂上漆卖出去——虽然不知道那是什么意思。\n\n你们简短商议，决定「相信」它会照做。果不其然，营地就在附近，剩下的守卫见你们人多势众，扔下营地四散而逃。你和[Companion Name]很快在他们的一顶帐篷里找到安娜，把她送回了家；贾斯和民兵则处理了另外十来个从乡间各地抓来的人。安娜的母亲在阿扎米尔郊外迎上你们，眼里含着泪，一遍又一遍地感谢你救了她女儿。"

msgid "With you and [Companion Name]'s help, you manage to break up the debris in short order, and Hapren directs much of the salvageable materials to be stored for reconstruction efforts, and the wood that is too mangled to be used to be left in the square to be used for the bonfire.\n\nJust as you set your tools down, a few tired looking folks make their way into the center of town, fishing gear in hand."
msgstr "在你和[Companion Name]的帮助下，残骸很快就清理完了；哈普伦让人把大部分还能用的材料存起来备重建之用，而那些损坏太严重、无法使用的木头则留在广场上，用来烧篝火。\n\n你刚放下工具，就有几个满脸疲惫的人提着渔具走进了镇中心。"

msgid "They stop their protesting as you grab their shoulder and pull them behind you. You know from all your time together they'd never really let you go by yourself, but as they grumble behind you, it's clear they're not pleased about running off to find... whatever is, up river.\n\nAfter a few minute jaunt upstream, you see it. A massive boar standing over a group of dead Golbins. It pulls against ropes that had been tied to trees along the river, and then thrown over the top of the beast. As you approach it catches sight of you both, assumes and breaks the last of its restrains as it charges towards you!"
msgstr "你抓住他们的肩膀、把人拉到身后，他们的抗议才停了下来。相处这么久，你知道他们绝不会真让你一个人去，但听着身后他们嘟囔的声音，显然对跑去上游找……不知道什么东西这件事很不满意。\n\n沿河向上走了几分钟，你看见了它。一头巨大的野猪站在一群死去的哥布林之上。它挣动着那些绑在河边树上、又从它背上绕过的绳索，在你走近时发现了你们俩，认定来意，挣断最后几道束缚，朝你们冲了过来！"

msgid "With the help of some villagers and their carts, you manage to bring back the Golbin's pet taming project. Hapren is shocked, then pleased, as he realizes that this is a far better catch than a few fish from the river.\n\nAs the sun sets, the wooden debris from the square is burnt and thick slabs of boar are grilled and given out to everyone in attendance. More and more curious folks poke their heads into the square and are met with warmth and light conversation.  A few folks even start up with light songs as the night progresses and Azamire's paltry stores of booze are enjoyed by those who indulge.\n\nAzamire's attack is far from forgotten, but this quiet moment amongst the survivors does well to begin healing the towns aching wounds."
msgstr "在几个村民和他们的推车帮助下，你们把哥布林那套驯养宠物的成果带了回来。哈普伦先是震惊，随即高兴起来——他意识到这比从河里捞几条鱼划算得多。\n\n太阳落山时，广场上的木料被点燃，厚厚的野猪肉被烤好分给在场的每一个人。越来越多好奇的人探头走进广场，被温暖和轻松的闲谈留了下来。夜色深了，几个兴致高的人还唱起了小调，阿扎米尔那点可怜的存酒也被愿意喝的人分着享受。\n\n阿扎米尔的劫难远未被忘记，但幸存者之间这个安静的夜晚，确实让镇子疼痛的伤口开始愈合。"

msgid "As you walk back into Azamire, you feel a swell of pride at the number of newly constructed buildings. They're small, and you hardly takes you long to count them on two hands, but still, Azamire is rebuilding, bit by bit.\n\nYour delight is interrupted by a shriek as you hear a... Golbin run by, chased by the newly appointed Militia Captain - Jass. The chase doesn't last long, and Gloob is held down while Jass berates it, talking about how she's no fool and knows a trap when she sees one."
msgstr "走回阿扎米尔时，看到新盖起的房屋，你心里涌起一阵自豪。它们都很小，两只手就数得过来，但阿扎米尔确实在一砖一瓦地重建。\n\n你的欣喜被一声尖叫打断——一只……哥布林跑了过去，后面追着新任的民兵队长贾斯。追逐没持续多久，格鲁布被按在地上，贾斯训斥着它，说自己可不是傻瓜，一眼就看得出那是陷阱。"

msgid "You manage to pull Jass aside long enough to get her to calm down. She apologies, first to you, then even to Gloob, and says that when she learned that they were capturing people to 'send them somewhere' it sent her over the edge. She asks Gloob to fill you in on what he told her. Every full moon, a bunch of robed figures end up coming to the Ringleader's fortress within the Elder Grove. They come with large, wooden wagons, and leave with people that the surrounding Golbin tribes have captured.\n\nHe goes on to say that the Golbins at the fortress leave with the robed figures, escorting them... wherever they go, he doesn't know. With the nearing full-moon, it'd be a great chance to get a peek into the fortress, and that he'd even go, but that he'd need some climbing gear and hooks to scale the fort's outer wall. Either hopefully or foolishly, you decide to trust him, and he details how he'd go about making the equipment. You and Jass decide it'd be good to bring [Companion Name] along as well, and that they'd go over Gloob's memory of the fort to plan the scouting mission while you make the gear."
msgstr "你总算把贾斯拉到一边，让她冷静下来。她先向你道歉，随后甚至也向格鲁布道了歉，说自己一听说他们抓人是要「送到什么地方去」，就压不住火了。她让格鲁布把对它说过的话再讲给你听：每个满月，都会有一群穿斗篷的人来到长老林里首领所在的堡垒。他们带着巨大的木车来，带走周边哥布林部族抓来的人。\n\n它接着说，堡垒里的哥布林会跟那些斗篷人一起离开，护送他们去……去哪它不知道。满月将近，正是窥探堡垒的好机会，它甚至愿意带路，但需要一些攀爬装备和钩子才能翻过外墙。不管是出于希望还是愚蠢，你决定相信它，它则详细说明了该怎么做出那套装备。你和贾斯决定把[Companion Name]也带上，由他们去核对格鲁布记忆里的堡垒布局、规划侦察路线，而你负责做装备。"

msgid "You, Gloob, and [Companion Name] set off into the Misty Thicket on the night of the full moon. Gloob brings you through the woods quickly, and it's tough to keep up with his speed. You and [Companion Name] find yourselves huffing and puffing just outside of the Ringleader's Fortress. In the moonlight, you all see a train of wagons and hobgolbins heading to the north along an old dirt road, but quickly lose track of it as they slip into the dense thicket.\n\nWith them gone, the three of you use the gear you prepared and scale the walls, landing quietly on the other side. Gloob brings you to several spots throughout the relatively open grounds. A small, ramshackle prison, with several ents patrolling just outside. You pass by a handful of sleeping areas for the fort's living guards, until you reach a large wooden hut Gloob says is the Ringleader's home. Finally, he leads you to a stockpile of various bits that a Golbin would find valuable, taken as tribute or looted from nearby towns. Hides, half-rotten food, weapons and armor, gold, and most notably, dozens upon dozens of caskets of flammable oil and booze.\n\nYou and [Companion Name] wait for Gloob to lead you into an ambush, but the trap never comes. True to his word, once he finishes with the important parts of the fortress, the three of you scale back over the wall and head back to Azamire. When you return, you immediately begin talks with Jass about launching an assault on the fortress with what you've learned, and set plans into motion to get the town ready. Clearing a path to bring wagons to the fort, and securing an exit route for prisoners will be essential before launching an attack. Plus, it gives Jass more time to get her people ready, too."
msgstr "满月之夜，你、格鲁布和[Companion Name]出发进入雾林。格鲁布在林中走得飞快，你几乎跟不上。等你们在首领的堡垒外停下来时，你和[Companion Name]都喘得厉害。月光下，你们看见一列车队和大哥布林沿着一条旧土路向北去，很快又消失进茂密的林子里。\n\n它们一走，你们三人便用备好的装备翻过墙头，悄无声息地落在另一侧。格鲁布带你们看了这片相对开阔场地上的几处地方：一座破败的小监狱，外面有几只树人在巡逻；几处堡垒守卫的睡处；直到一座大木屋，格鲁布说那是首领的住处。最后，它把你们带到一堆哥布林觉得值钱的东西前——贡品或从附近镇子抢来的战利品：兽皮、半腐的食物、武器与护甲、金子，最惹眼的是成打成打的木桶，装着易燃的油和酒。\n\n你和[Companion Name]等着格鲁布把你们引进埋伏，但陷阱始终没有出现。它说到做到，带你们看完堡垒要紧的地方后，三人翻墙回去，返回阿扎米尔。回来后你立刻跟贾斯谈如何根据所见发起进攻，并着手准备：打通能让推车靠近堡垒的道路、为俘虏安排好撤离路线，这些在开战前都是必须的。这也顺便给了贾斯更多时间把她的人练好。"

msgid "Late in the evening, you head to the recently built home for [Companion Name]. It's nothing fancy - like most of the new constructions in Azamire - but all of the folks who've been contributing the most were given priority in separate lodgings, and they've done wonders for bringing back a bit of normalcy.\n\nWhat hasn't been normal is how little you've seen [Companion Name] lately. You've had plenty of times where you weren't attached at the hip over the years you've known one another, but you know they've been around. It almost feels as if they've been avoiding you.\n\nYou knock several times to no avail. Just as you turn to go, you see a limping figure approach, notice you, and then turn away."
msgstr "夜里很晚时，你前往[Companion Name]新近建成的住处。房子不怎么起眼——和阿扎米尔大多数新建筑一样——但出力最多的人都优先分到了独立住所，这些对恢复一点正常生活起了很大作用。\n\n不正常的是一直很少见到[Companion Name]。相识这些年，你们也有过不黏在一起的时候，但你知道他们就在附近。几乎感觉像在躲着你。\n\n你敲了好几次门，没有回应。正要转身离开时，你看见一个跛行的身影走近，注意到你，又转身走开。"

msgid "[Companion Name] turns towards you and wobbles on their feet. Even in the low light, you notice the dark red patch blood on the front of their cloak, and trailing down their arms. You rush towards them and manage to catch your best friend before they hit the ground. You quickly run through a list of places you could bring them before settling on their own place. You quickly fish their key out of their pocket and carry them inside. You'd complain about them being heavy if it weren't for the fact your heart was beating out of your chest, knowing how hurt they are and having no idea on why or how.\n\nDigging through both their supplies and yours, you find enough to get them patched up. Across their chest is a large gash with bits of... wood, sticking out of it? You extract it all, bit by bit, in the lantern light, and stitch them back up before wrapping them in gauze. The rest of their wounds are comparatively minor, and take much less time to deal with, but they are numerous, and in various states of healing, some old, some fresh.\n\nOnce you're done, [Companion Name] looks more mummy than person, but they'll live. You cover them up to let them rest, and decide to help along their recovery with their favorite food."
msgstr "[Companion Name]朝你转过来，脚下晃了晃。即便光线很暗，你还是看见他们斗篷前襟上暗红的血迹，一路拖到手臂。你冲过去，在最好的朋友倒下之前接住了他们。你飞快地把能去的地方过了一遍，最后决定回他们自己家。你从他们口袋里摸出钥匙，把人抱了进去。要不是心脏几乎要跳出胸口，你本来会抱怨他们真沉——你不知道他们伤得多重，也不知道是怎么伤的、为什么。\n\n你翻遍他们的和你的补给，凑出足够处理伤口的东西。胸口是一道很长的裂口，里面还嵌着些……木头？在提灯的光下，你一点一点把它们取出来，缝合，再用纱布包好。其余的伤相对较轻，处理起来快得多，但数量很多，愈合程度各不相同，有旧伤也有新伤。\n\n弄完之后，[Companion Name]看起来更像木乃伊而不是人，但命保住了。你替他们盖好被子让他们休息，决定用他们最爱吃的东西帮着恢复。"

msgid "They detail the events of the night. How they came across the creature, and the talismans in its branches flashed with a bright blue light as they tried to run away. How they floated up into the air and were sucked towards the ent while they flailed about in the air, and then how the ent sent them flying after the talismans in its branches flashed bright blue. [Companion Name] was sure they were going to die, until they saw that the talismans in the ent's branches matched the similar charms forming a line in the nearby treeline. The giant ent shuffled back and forth at that line, but wouldn't cross it. Then, they limped all the way back to Azamire.\n\nAfter a through amount of ridicule and chastisement, you hug them and tell them you're glad they're okay.\n\nIn the morning you detail everything that happened to Jass, who gathers up the archers of her militia and send them out with you and a wounded [Companion Name], who leads you to the grove with the giant ent. It seems that it has been joined by several of the smaller ones, but you aren't dissuaded. "
msgstr "他们讲述了那晚的经过：如何遇到那个生物，在他们想逃走时，它枝干上的护符闪出亮蓝的光；如何漂浮到空中、在空中挣扎着被吸向那个树人；然后在护符亮起蓝光之后，树人如何把他们甩飞出去。[Companion Name]确信自己要死了，直到发现那树人枝上的护符与附近林线上一串相似符咒排成一线相互对应。那巨大树人在那条线前来回踱动，却不肯越过。之后，他们一路跛行回了阿扎米尔。\n\n在一通彻底的嘲笑与数落之后，你抱住他们，说你很高兴他们没事。\n\n早上，你把发生的一切详细告诉贾斯；她召集民兵中的弓箭手，让他们与你以及带伤的[Companion Name]一同出发——由后者带你们去那棵巨大树人所在的林子。看来已有几个较小的树人加入了它，但你没有退缩。 "

msgid "As you walk through Azamire, the town is abuzz with nervous energy. Several wagons are lined up and everyone who isn't fighting have come out to wish you well. Hapren approaches, and mentions that the town has gotten together and prepared some combat supplies into the back of one of the carts for you, and hopes that it helps.\n\nYou all set off, and as the sun begins to set, the cold mist of the thicket starts to seep into your clothes. The militia is tense, but ready. There are people to save, and taking out the Ringleader would go a long way towards making everyone safer."
msgstr "走在阿扎米尔街头，镇子里弥漫着紧张的气息。几辆推车排成一列，没参战的人都出来为你送行。哈普伦走过来，说镇上给大家准备了一些战斗补给，已经装在其中一辆车的后面，希望派得上用场。\n\n你们出发了。太阳开始西沉，林子的冷雾渐渐渗进衣服。民兵们很紧张，但都准备好了。有人等着被救，而干掉首领，能让大家安全得多。"

msgid "Alarms start to sound as the militia's arrows are lit. You clutch your weapon in anticipation, wishing you could to go check on the tunnel to see how Gloob's breakout went, but there's no time. The hillside is lit up with the fires you and [Companion Name] started, and hobgolbins on the wall begin to shoot towards you. But it's too late. Burning arrow after arrow soar up and over the wall, towards where you pointed out the stockpile. No one can see over the wall, so it's tough to tell if anyone is on target until a resounding BOOM make you cover your ears, even from this far away.\n\nMany of the defenders are thrown from the wall entirely, and as you and the militia charge, the swordsmen dispatch the stunned hobgolbins that fell on the wrong side of the wall. Arrows start to fall again, as the fort's guards gather themselves, and they're met with your militia's own volleys."
msgstr "民兵的箭被点燃时，警报响起。你握紧武器等待，很想跑去隧道看看格鲁布的突袭进展如何，但已经没时间了。山坡被你和[Companion Name]点起的火光照亮，墙上的大哥布林开始朝你们射击。但已经太迟了。一支又一支火箭越过城墙，飞向你指出的那堆物资。没人能看穿城墙，很难判断是否命中，直到一声轰然巨响让你捂住耳朵——即便隔着这么远。\n\n许多守军直接被掀下墙头；你和民兵冲上去时，剑士们结果了那些摔在墙内侧、还没回过神的哥布林。堡垒的守卫缓过劲来，箭雨再次落下，迎接他们的是民兵的齐射。"

msgid "The occasional pained grunt, or worse, the painted gurgles of someone who was struck somewhere lethal, dampen your mood. You knew people would fall today. You can only imagine how the people on the hillside are faring. Just as your mind starts to lose focus, thinking about those you'd lose, you see a burning light at the end of your axe. As you pull it back, you realize you're through! You give a cheer that turns into a battlecry, and your group follows suit. A few more axe strikes and enough holes are opened to let Azamire's troops push through the gate.\n\nThe fort grounds are... hellish. Most of the ent guardians already crawl on the ground, crying out with groaning wails as they burn, with nearly every structure already completely engulfed in flames. You wonder for a moment if there's even a point of being inside until a massive blue Golbin covered in singed fabric cries out as he locks eyes with you. The rest of the fort's surviving defenders stand in the middle of the blazing stronghold with the Ringleader, smashing weapons against their shields, waiting for orders. "
msgstr "偶尔传来的痛苦闷哼，或者更糟的、被击中要害的人喉咙里的咕噜声，让你的心情沉下去。你知道今天会有人倒下。你只能猜想山坡上的人现在如何。就在你的心神开始涣散、想着会失去谁时，你看见斧刃尽头亮起一团火光。你把它往后一拉，才意识到自己砍穿了！你发出一声欢呼，随即变成战吼，你那队人跟着吼了起来。又几斧落下，洞口开得够大，阿扎米尔的队伍终于能涌过城门。\n\n堡垒的场地简直是地狱。大多数树人守卫已经在地上爬行，烧着，发出呻吟般的哀鸣；几乎所有建筑都已被火舌吞没。你有一瞬间怀疑进去到底还有没有意义——直到一只浑身焦布、体格巨大的蓝色哥布林看见你，放声大喊。堡垒里残存的守卫与首领一起站在燃烧的堡垒中央，用武器敲着盾牌，等待命令。"

msgid "Not a single person falters as they stream past you, charging with weapons and heads held high. You don't turn away as you see some being driven through as the Ringleader's forces crash into your own. Time slows as you push through, trusting your people to keep you safe. As you make it through the bodies, the Ringleader stands with a gnarled smirk, holding what must be half a burning tree as its weapon, seemingly unbothered by the flames that flicker up its arm.\n\nYou hear people roar in the battle behind you, some in victory, others... likely as their last act of defiance against the opposing force. You steel yourself and step forward, challenging the Ringleader."
msgstr "没有人迟疑，他们从你身边涌过，举着武器、昂着头冲锋。当首领的部队撞上你们的人，你看见有人被刺穿，也没有转过头去。时间仿佛变慢，你向前推进，把自己的安危交给身边的人。等你从尸体间穿出，首领带着扭曲的笑站着，手里举着一棵还在燃烧的半截树当武器，手臂上窜起的火焰似乎丝毫没影响到它。\n\n你听见身后战场上的怒吼，有些是胜利的，有些……大概是他们最后的顽抗。你稳住心神，迈步上前，向首领挑战。"

msgid "Before you lies the broken body of the Ringleader, sickly purple blood spilling from his wounds. You finally spare a glance to those around you, and you realize... it's over. Less than half the attacking force remains, but Azamire's people still stand.  Gloob stands among the militia, deep green body covered in the blue blood of hobgolbins, and he lets out a cheer, one that the remaining militia proudly meet. Jass barks out orders, pointing out wounded with the stump of her arm, then starting to pull one of the wounded towards the gate with her other.\n\nHalf a dozen emotions cross [Companion Name]'s face the second you look at them, but most among them all, relief. They embrace you for naught but a moment before heading towards the Ringleader, who barely manages a ragged breath. As you approach, the beast lets out a throaty cackle before it devolves into a choking cough. You ask it two questions. Where did the shipments go, and who are the people it works for?\n\nHe just sits and smirks, the flames of his burning fortress dancing in his eyes.\n\n\"They'll come back soon.\""
msgstr "你面前是头目破碎的躯体，病态紫色的血从伤口里涌出。你这才有空看一眼周围的人，然后意识到——结束了。进攻的队伍剩下不到一半，但阿扎米尔的人还站着。格鲁布站在民兵中间，深绿的身体浸满大哥布林的蓝血，它发出一声欢呼，剩下的民兵也自豪地应和。贾斯用残臂指着伤员，大声下令，另一只手已经开始把一个伤者往城门方向拖。\n\n你一看向[Companion Name]，六七种情绪便掠过他们的脸，其中最浓的是释然。他们只抱了你一瞬，就走向头目——后者勉强喘着一口气。你靠近时，那头野兽发出一阵低沉的怪笑，随后变成窒息的咳嗽。你问它两个问题：那些货去了哪里，以及它在为谁卖命？\n\n它只是坐着笑，眼里跳动着燃烧堡垒的火光。\n\n「他们很快就会回来。」"

